---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LoadProfile from "../components/LoadProfile.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import { site, education } from "../data/site";
import { certifications, skills } from "../data/experience";

const featured = certifications.filter((c) => c.featured);
---

<Base>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-10 pb-4 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_320px] lg:items-end lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <h1 class="max-w-[16ch] text-display font-extrabold text-balance">
          I’m an energy engineer who enjoys turning complex systems into clear, useful knowledge.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[54ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-forest/90 sm:text-xl">
          {site.role} at Energy Sciences. I audit industrial and commercial facilities, study how energy moves through equipment and processes, and publish what I learn. This site is where I share practical explanations, lessons from the field, and ideas that can help the industry operate more efficiently and sustainably.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-x-6 gap-y-4 lg:grid-cols-1 lg:gap-y-5 lg:pb-1">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs text-forest-soft">Based in</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 font-semibold">{site.location}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs text-forest-soft">Audits led</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 font-semibold tnum">10+ ASHRAE I–III</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-xs text-forest-soft">Credentials</dt>
          <dd class="mt-0.5 font-semibold">CEM, LEED GA, EIT</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <LoadProfile />
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a
        href="/experience"
        class="rounded-md bg-emerald px-5 py-3 text-[0.95rem] font-semibold text-deep transition-colors hover:bg-emerald-deep hover:text-mist"
      >
        See the work
      </a>
      <a
        href={site.resume}
        download
        class="rounded-md border border-line-strong px-5 py-3 text-[0.95rem] font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-emerald-deep hover:text-emerald-deep"
      >
        Download resume
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section id="about" class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8 sm:mt-28">

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_300px] lg:gap-16">
      <div class="max-w-[66ch] space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I work on the unglamorous middle of decarbonization: the compressed air line that leaks,
          the air handler that runs at full speed all night, the process heater nobody has trended
          since commissioning. Finding those is a measurement problem before it is an engineering
          problem, which is where my training comes in.
        </p>
        <p>
          My <strong class="font-semibold">M.S. in Industrial Engineering</strong> at West Virginia
          University was built around quantitative analysis — regression modeling in R and Python,
          large public datasets, and the statistics needed to defend a savings number to a utility
          reviewer. My thesis used U.S. county-level socio-economic and demographic data to understand how
          socioeconomic and demographic factors shape energy consumption. It produced one
          peer-reviewed paper and a review article.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside that, I ran more than a dozen ASHRAE Level I–II assessments through the WVU
          Pollution Prevention Lab. Today I do the same work at Energy Sciences: on-site
          assessment, custom savings calculations, incentive validation, and post-install Measurement and Verification.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before the U.S., I designed solar arrays and pumping systems with SunFarmer Nepal and
          studied the economics of moving Nepal's motorcycle fleet off gasoline. That work still
          shapes how I think about efficiency — as something that has to pencil out for the people
          paying for it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Education</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            {
              education.map((e) => (
                <li class="border-l-2 border-emerald pl-3.5">
                  <p class="font-semibold">{e.degree}</p>
                  <p class="text-sm text-forest-soft">
                    {e.school}, {e.place}
                  </p>
                  <p class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-forest-soft tnum">
                    {e.years} &middot; {e.detail}
                  </p>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Credentials</h3>
          <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
            {
              featured.map((c) => (
                <li
                  class="rounded border border-line-strong px-2.5 py-1 text-sm font-semibold"
                  title={`${c.name} — ${c.issuer}`}
                >
                  {c.abbr}
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm text-forest-soft">
            <a href="/experience#certifications" class="link-underline">Full list with issuers</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Capability -->
  <section class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8 sm:mt-28">
    <SectionHeading title="What I work with" as="h2" />
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        skills.map((s) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">{s.group}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-forest-soft">{s.items.join(", ")}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
